<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="8f28077a">What is a control? 
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        A control is defined as any action taken to mitigate or manage risk and increase the probability that the
        business/process will achieve its goals and objectives.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Controls are specific steps in the process so that the relevant objectives are accomplished and relevant resources
        are protected.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        They serve as risk mitigants.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        They play a critical role in meeting compliance requirements, as they are the effective means through which
        compliance is justified, tested and reported.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Lack of controls can lead to non-compliance, which has potential legal and/or regulatory ramifications for the
        organization.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Nature of controls
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;h4&gt;
            Preventive
        &lt;/h4&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    &lt;p style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
        Control activities designed to prevent the occurrence of an error or irregularity that would materially affect the
        achievement of the company&apos;s objectives. e.g., system access.
    &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;h4&gt;
            Detective
        &lt;/h4&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    &lt;p style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
        Control activities designed to detect and correct in a timely manner an error or irregularity that would materially
        affect the achievement of the company&apos;s objectives, e.g., review of error reports.
    &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;h4&gt;
            Corrective
        &lt;/h4&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    &lt;p style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
        Control activities intended to limit the damage caused by an incident, e. g., business continuity.
    &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Types of controls
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;h4&gt;
            Manual
        &lt;/h4&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
        Controls performed by individuals manually e.g., reconciliations.
    &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;h4&gt;
            IT Dependent Manual
        &lt;/h4&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
        Control based on manual procedures that are supported by or dependent on IT systems (such as system-generated
        reports).
    &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;h4&gt;
            Automated
        &lt;/h4&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
        Controls performed by an application, e.g., built in system authority limits.
    &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;div style=&quot;MARGIN-LEFT: 2em&quot;&gt;
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                &lt;strong&gt;Configurable or Embedded&lt;/strong&gt;
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;
            Control based on configuration setup(s) within the application.
        &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
    &lt;div style=&quot;MARGIN-LEFT: 2em&quot;&gt;
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                &lt;h4&gt;
                    Inherent System
                &lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;
            Control based on inherent functionality within the application.
        &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
    &lt;div style=&quot;MARGIN-LEFT: 2em&quot;&gt;
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
                &lt;h4&gt;
                    Custom Programs
                &lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;
            Control based on functionality of custom programs developed for the application.
        &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Control categories
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;h4&gt;
            Entry Level Controls (ELCs)
        &lt;/h4&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div style=&quot;MARGIN-LEFT: 2em&quot;&gt;
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                &lt;h4&gt;
                    Direct entry level control (ELCs)
                &lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;
            Controls that have a direct relationship to the effectiveness of transaction-level controls. Such controls
            might be designed to identify lower level control weaknesses, and when operating effectively, might allow for a
            reduction in the testing of transaction-level controls, e.g., a financial reconciliation.
        &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
    &lt;div style=&quot;MARGIN-LEFT: 2em&quot;&gt;
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                &lt;h4&gt;
                    Indirect entry level controls (ELCs)
                &lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;
            Controls that have an indirect relationship to the control objective, but can affect the nature, timing and
            extent of procedures performed on other controls e.g., policies, codes of conduct, the organization&apos;s
            governance structure.
        &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;h4&gt;
            Transaction-level controls
        &lt;/h4&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
        Controls that function at a detailed transaction-level such as edit checks, validations, calculations,
        authorizations and segregation of duties.
    &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;h4&gt;
            IT General Controls
        &lt;/h4&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
        Controls that function at the level of information systems to&amp;nbsp;check that the system is operating in a
        consistent and reliable manner.
    &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;div style=&quot;MARGIN-LEFT: 2em&quot;&gt;
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                &lt;h4&gt;
                    Manage Change
                &lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;
            Controls over making changes to the IT environment including IT application programs, configurations and report
            logic.
        &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
    &lt;div style=&quot;MARGIN-LEFT: 2em&quot;&gt;
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                &lt;h4&gt;
                    Manage Access
                &lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;
            Controls over access to the various IT environment components.
        &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
    &lt;div style=&quot;MARGIN-LEFT: 2em&quot;&gt;
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                &lt;h4&gt;
                    Manage IT Operations
                &lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;blockquote style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot;&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;
            Controls over processing environment and preparing for routine equipment and software failures that could
            affect complete and accurate financial statement transaction processing.
        &lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Frequency of controls
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Frequency of execution of the control (multiple times daily, daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, semi-annually,
        annually, on-demand).
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The frequency of control activities has a direct impact on the sample size during testing.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Control environment framework
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The image 1 below depicts a control environment framework with a mix of manual and automated controls, which is
        typical at a client. This framework also depicts the dependence of all automated and IT dependent manual controls
        on a functioning IT general control environment which includes the operating system, databases, and the
        infrastructure elements.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Image 1: control environment framework&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    &lt;img alt=&quot;Control Environment Framework&quot; src=&quot;./../../../core.gen.common.base/guidances/concepts/./resources/control framework.jpg&quot; width=&quot;700&quot; height=&quot;600&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
